{"name":"Espalier","hex":"#2f5f3a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"espalier","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A latticework used to shape or train the branches of a tree or shrub into a two-dimensional ornamental or useful design, as along a wall or fence.","A plant that has been shaped in this manner."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To train a plant in this manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/espalier"}],"entries":[{"title":"Espalier","blocks":[{"text":"Espalier is the horticultural and ancient agricultural practice of controlling woody plant growth for the production of fruit, by pruning and tying branches to a frame. Plants are frequently shaped in formal patterns, flat against a structure such as a wall, fence, or trellis. The term is also used to refer to plants which have been shaped in this way."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Horizontal_espalier.JPG/330px-Horizontal_espalier.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Espalier"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Espalier_fruit_tree_at_Standen%2C_West_Sussex%2C_England_May_2006.JPG/500px-Espalier_fruit_tree_at_Standen%2C_West_Sussex%2C_England_May_2006.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Espalier_fruit_tree_at_Standen%2C_West_Sussex%2C_England_May_2006.JPG/1280px-Espalier_fruit_tree_at_Standen%2C_West_Sussex%2C_England_May_2006.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Espalier_fruit_tree_at_Standen%2C_West_Sussex%2C_England_May_2006.JPG/500px-Espalier_fruit_tree_at_Standen%2C_West_Sussex%2C_England_May_2006.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Free-standing espaliered fruit trees (step-over) at Standen, West Sussex. The trees are used to create a fruit border or low hedge.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEspalier_fruit_tree_at_Standen%2C_West_Sussex%2C_England_May_2006.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Espalier_-_Belgian_fence.jpg/500px-Espalier_-_Belgian_fence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Espalier_-_Belgian_fence.jpg/500px-Espalier_-_Belgian_fence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEspalier_-_Belgian_fence.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/01212belgianfenceinice.JPG/500px-01212belgianfenceinice.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/01212belgianfenceinice.JPG/1280px-01212belgianfenceinice.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/01212belgianfenceinice.JPG/500px-01212belgianfenceinice.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A01212belgianfenceinice.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/DSCN3598_espalieredpeartree_e.JPG/500px-DSCN3598_espalieredpeartree_e.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/DSCN3598_espalieredpeartree_e.JPG/500px-DSCN3598_espalieredpeartree_e.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A pear tree espaliered into a cordon. The picture was taken in the garden of the Cloisters in upper Manhattan.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADSCN3598_espaliere